      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__sl__bt__pawr__advertiser_1gaf9bfde544c3a6c5598df4a87b174e83b" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>sl_status_t</type>
        <definition>sl_status_t sl_bt_pawr_advertiser_create_connection</definition>
        <argsstring>(uint8_t advertising_set, uint8_t subevent, bd_addr address, uint8_t address_type, uint8_t *connection)</argsstring>
        <name>sl_bt_pawr_advertiser_create_connection</name>
        <param>
          <type>uint8_t</type>
          <declname>advertising_set</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>uint8_t</type>
          <declname>subevent</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="structbd__addr" kindref="compound">bd_addr</ref></type>
          <declname>address</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>uint8_t</type>
          <declname>address_type</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>uint8_t *</type>
          <declname>connection</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Initiate a connection request to a device that is synchronized to the specified active PAwR train. The connection is established on the secondary PHY configured for the advertising set with the <ref refid="group__sl__bt__extended__advertiser_1gac7a6395d280c76bb3396ce6182c9d1ca" kindref="member">sl_bt_extended_advertiser_set_phy</ref> command. The connection uses the parameters configured with command <ref refid="group__sl__bt__connection_1gac2453ab6efcbfc71b3bb23b3fffce1df" kindref="member">sl_bt_connection_set_default_parameters</ref>.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">advertising_set</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The PAwR advertising set handle </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">subevent</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The subevent in which the connection request is to be sent </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">address</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Address of the device to connect to </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">address_type</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Enum <ref refid="group__sl__bt__gap_1gac8d5431d3062e47c5d51b9fb9f36c104" kindref="member">sl_bt_gap_address_type_t</ref>. Address type of the device to connect to. Values:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><bold>sl_bt_gap_public_address (0x0):</bold> Public device address</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>sl_bt_gap_static_address (0x1):</bold> Static device address</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>sl_bt_gap_random_resolvable_address (0x2):</bold> Resolvable private random address</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>sl_bt_gap_random_nonresolvable_address (0x3):</bold> Non-resolvable private random address</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>sl_bt_gap_public_address_resolved_from_rpa (0x4):</bold> Public identity address resolved from a resolvable private address (RPA)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>sl_bt_gap_static_address_resolved_from_rpa (0x5):</bold> Static identity address resolved from a resolvable private address (RPA) </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="out">connection</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Handle that will be assigned to the connection after the connection is established. This handle is valid only if the result code of this command is SL_STATUS_OK.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>SL_STATUS_OK if successful. Error code otherwise.</para>
</simplesect>
<bold>Events</bold> <itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><ref refid="group__sl__bt__evt__connection__closed" kindref="compound">sl_bt_evt_connection_closed</ref> - This event is triggered if the connection failed to be created.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><ref refid="group__sl__bt__evt__connection__opened" kindref="compound">sl_bt_evt_connection_opened</ref> - This event is triggered after the connection is opened and indicates whether the devices are already bonded and the role of the device in this connection.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><ref refid="group__sl__bt__evt__connection__parameters" kindref="compound">sl_bt_evt_connection_parameters</ref> - This event indicates the connection parameters and security mode of the connection. </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
